NOTE (must resolve before public release): drop the verbatim text of the
GNU GPL v2 into LICENSES/GPL-2.0-or-later.txt. It is intentionally NOT
reproduced from memory here — an inexact copy of a legal text is worse
than an explicit pointer. Fetch the canonical text from
https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.txt

Licensing rationale (see memory/engine.md §0.1): the upstream
ppf-contact-solver is Apache-2.0, which is compatible with GPLv3 but not
GPLv2-only. Conveying the combined work under "GPL v2-or-later" lets it be
distributed under GPLv3 terms, making the Apache-2.0 (ppf) and Apache/MIT
(wgpu) code legally combinable. Every third-party dependency must be one of
{MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, MPL-2.0, GPLv2+, GPLv3}. Reject GPLv2-only,
non-commercial, or research-only licenses.
